  "rationale": "Two direct-match candidates for otosclerosis are present (PGS001255 and PGS002046), both trained in UK Biobank and both aligned on trait_efo=otosclerosis. PGS001255 is preferred because it provides more directly comparable discrimination metrics in the context (PGS-only AUROC=0.6319 with CI and full-model AUROC=0.6532; plus PGS-only R2=0.01341), enabling a clearer assessment than PGS002046, which reports only partial correlation (partial-r=0.0182) and has AUC/R2 fields null. However, confidence is low and outcome is sub-optimal because both candidates come from high-throughput UKB framework/portability publications rather than disease-focused otosclerosis studies, and PGS001255 uses a time-to-event endpoint (phenotyping_reported: TTE otosclerosis), which the provided domain guidance notes should be down-ranked unless counterbalanced by stronger disease-focused evidence that is not available here."
